Subject: Competitive play: a set's game announces its search at once
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

DWC's RANKED search first waits until the master server lists the game's own
session with its matchmaking keys, which the game sends in a state-changed
heartbeat. QR2 sends one at most every 10 seconds, and the game had just sent
its first when it logged in, so a set's search sat for about 9 seconds before
it looked for the opponent (reservations wait the same way). While a set's
game searches RANKED, qr2_send_statechanged now asks the module
(src/platform/competitive_match.cpp) and sends the heartbeat at once; the
master server is Recharged's own.

diff --git a/src/RVL_SDK/gamespy/qr2/qr2.c b/src/RVL_SDK/gamespy/qr2/qr2.c
--- a/src/RVL_SDK/gamespy/qr2/qr2.c
+++ b/src/RVL_SDK/gamespy/qr2/qr2.c
@@ -6,6 +6,11 @@
 #include "../common/gsCommon.h"
 #include "../natneg/natneg.h"
 #include "qr2regkeys.h"
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+/* Competitive play (src/platform/competitive_match.cpp): nonzero while a
+   set's game searches RANKED (tweak patch 0056). */
+int mscharged_competitive_announce_now(void);
+#endif
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 extern "C" {
@@ -538,6 +543,16 @@
                   "Requested send statechange for LAN game, discarding\r\n");
     return;
   }
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+  /* Competitive play: a set's search waits for its own listing, and the
+     opponent's for its reservation; Recharged's master server takes each
+     change at once rather than 10 seconds after the last heartbeat. */
+  if (mscharged_competitive_announce_now()) {
+    send_heartbeat(qrec, 1);
+    qrec->userstatechangerequested = 0;
+    return;
+  }
+#endif
   if (current_time() - qrec->lastheartbeat < MIN_STATECHANGED_HB_TIME) {
     gsDebugFormat(GSIDebugCat_QR2, GSIDebugType_Misc, GSIDebugLevel_Notice,
                   "Queing statechange for later send (too soon)\r\n");
